Employee Handbook (NDS-HR-HB-001 v2.0, current, effective 2026-10-01)
16 Whistleblowing and reporting concerns > 16.3 How to raise a concern

Concerns can be raised with any of the following:

- the employee's line manager or Head of Department;

- the Head of Risk and Compliance (compliance@northstar.example);

- speakup@northstar.example;

- the independent **Speak Up line** , operated by an independent third-party provider and available 24/7 by web form and telephone via the intranet, which accepts anonymous reports.

Concerns involving a manager or Director should be raised with someone outside their reporting line or through the Speak Up line. Concerns involving the Chief Executive Officer should be raised with the Chair of the Audit Committee via the Speak Up line. Workers may also report to an appropriate prescribed person or body (for example, a regulator), as permitted by law.

